    {
      "path": "src/world-scroll.h",
      "name": "world-scroll.h",
      "kind": "source",
      "source": "#include <stdint.h>\n#define WEB64_SCROLL_NONE 0\n#define WEB64_SCROLL_LEFT 1\n#define WEB64_SCROLL_RIGHT 2\n#define WEB64_SCROLL_UP 3\n#define WEB64_SCROLL_DOWN 4\nvoid asm_world_scroll_init(void);\n_fastcall void asm_world_scroll_step(uint8_t direction);\nvoid asm_world_scroll_present(void);\nuint16_t asm_world_scroll_pixel_x(void);\nuint16_t asm_world_scroll_pixel_y(void);\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "TEMPLATE.md",
      "name": "TEMPLATE.md",
      "kind": "source",
      "source": "# World Horizontal Scroller\n\nA smooth joystick-controlled horizontal World scroller with transactional double buffering and stable region Color RAM.\n\n## Architecture Notes: Why this architecture?\n\nC owns input and tick order; a generated assembly renderer prepares a complete next viewport offscreen and does not reuse either page until the staged VIC presentation is committed.\n\nThe project uses Build Targets so artifact policy stays out of source code. Native assets remain editable and generated C/assembly bindings describe the same bytes. Optional runtime modules are target scoped and dead-strip when they are not selected.\n\n### Change these decisions when\n\n- profiling identifies a measured hot path or memory collision;\n- the target hardware, video standard, or artifact type changes;\n- a project-specific renderer has outgrown the generic extension hook.\n\n### Keep these decisions when\n\n- the change only hides C64 hardware behavior behind another abstraction;\n- it would duplicate bytes already owned by a native Web64 asset;\n- it would move frame-critical work from a bounded assembly path into an unmeasured loop.\n\n## First Modification\n\nEdit the native world map and charset while preserving the measured buffered renderer; use the static template when every map cell needs a distinct color.\n\n## Project Contract\n\n- Entry: main.c\n- Language: Mixed\n- Compiler ABI: web64-stack-v1\n- Video: PAL\n- Native assets: .w64chr, .w64blk, .w64map, .w64spr\n- Compatibility modules: none\n- Character mode: mono\n- Color RAM: region\n- Camera bounds: clamp\n\n\n## References\n\n- semantic-inspiration: [Commodore 64 Programmer Reference Guide](https://archive.org/details/c64-programmer-ref)\n\nThis file belongs to the generated project. Updating the bundled template never mutates this project.\n"
    }
  ]
